Optional polish: add a "Claude Mode" entry to nocturne-ui's General settings.

The primary mode switch needs no source patch — `scripts/inject-firmware.js`
grafts `switch.js` into the built music UI, and holding preset 1 + preset 4 for
one second toggles between `/` and `/claude/`. This patch is for users who build
nocturne-ui from source anyway and want a visible menu entry too.

Apply in the nocturne workspace:

    cd ~/Desktop/Projects/nocturne/nocturne-ui
    git apply ../../claude-thing/patches/nocturne-ui-claude-mode.patch

Two edits in `src/components/settings/Settings.jsx`, both mirroring the existing
`factory-reset` action item:

1. In the General section's `items` array (immediately before the
   `id: "factory-reset"` entry, ~line 100):

```jsx
      {
        id: "claude-mode",
        title: "Claude Mode",
        type: "action",
        description:
          "Switch to the Claude Code session monitor. Hold preset 1 + preset 4 to come back.",
        action: "claudeMode",
      },
```

2. In `handleAction` (~line 670), a new case beside `factoryReset`:

```jsx
      case "claudeMode":
        try {
          window.localStorage.setItem("claude-mode", "1");
        } catch (e) {}
        window.location.assign("/claude/");
        break;
```

No other changes. `/claude/` is served from the same origin by nocturned's
static server, so this is a plain same-origin navigation; the Claude app's
"Exit to Music" action (and the preset chord) clears the `claude-mode` flag so
the device boots back into music mode.

NOTE: documented as an edit rather than a byte-exact diff because line numbers
in Settings.jsx shift between nocturne releases.
